For H2, one useful claim does have an elementary proof: two distinct relations whose product is a square always give a proper factor when \(T=o(\sqrt N)\). Linear algebra does not guarantee a dependency of size two. For longer dependencies, I have not found a way to control the \(N\)-dependent kernel; fixed-test Jacobi cancellation leaves that step unresolved.
